# The repository's own gate, run against what is actually being committed.
#
# lint-staged hides unstaged work for the duration, so the typecheck inside it
# reads the index rather than the working tree — which is what makes the check
# mean "this commit compiles", not "this laptop happens to compile right now".
# It also formats and lints the staged files in place, so a commit is always
# the shape dprint and eslint would give it.
pnpm exec lint-staged
